00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.470
I'm unbelievably humbled to
be speaking at this event,

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.040
just what an extraordinary
collection of people,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.450
and I hope I get to
say hello to all of you

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.700
before I get out of here.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.712
What I'm about to talk about
is predicated on the fact that

00:00:48.712 --> 00:00:50.683
over the last three to four years,

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:55.683
off of a pretty sizable base of followers,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.599
engagers on social, my
awareness grew exponentially

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:03.660
over platforms that skewed younger,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.791
and as my attention on
Instagram and YouTube

00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:11.502
grew aggressively over these 36 months,

00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:14.370
what ended up happening
was a lot of the people

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.720
I was interacting with got younger,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.160
and younger, and younger.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.160
What I want to talk about today
is predicated on me reading

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.880
hundreds of thousands of direct messages

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.810
over the last three years.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.890
What I want to talk about
today is not predicated on

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.950
my opinion, it's an
observation from one person,

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.940
one man's point of view.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.120
It's also the observation of somebody

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.260
who is so deeply grateful
for the remarkable way

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:46.260
that I feel that my mother
parented me, and my father,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.520
and the circumstances of being
an immigrant born in Belarus

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.170
coming to United States and
going through that struggle.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:58.202
I believe that so much of
what every single person

00:01:58.202 --> 00:02:02.243
in this audience cares deeply
about trying to affect,

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.300
and so many of the characteristics

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.543
that we are passionate
about, whether it's empathy,

00:02:07.543 --> 00:02:11.160
or kindness, or gratitude, needs to have

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.070
a remarkable conversation
with ourselves around a word

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.760
called entitlement.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.620
Entitlement is not privilege.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.720
Entitlement is a very
important word for all of us,

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.830
because it is foundational
in the starting point

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.890
to all the other things
we've been talking about

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.880
over the last two days.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.000
Entitlement is also
gonna be very difficult

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.680
for all of us to talk about in this room

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.120
because it means we have
to look at ourselves,

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.100
not look at the people
that we're imposing it on.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.320
Over the last three years,
I have received hundreds

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.720
of thousands of messages
from 15-25 year olds

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:51.510
telling me variations of
stories of how much they love

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.360
and appreciate their parents
deeply, but deep down,

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.920
they resent them and, or hate them so much

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.010
because while they continue
to take their Unlimited Uber

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.820
from their parents, while
they continue to take

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.650
a brand new BMW on their 17th birthday,

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.200
while they continue to be thrilled

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.360
that their parents bought
them their first apartment

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.330
in New York City, or much smaller things,

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.630
like a first class plane ticket,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.940
or something of that
degree, they inherently

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.270
deeply understand that
they are a zoo animal,

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.683
and are completely unprepared
to actually live in the world.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.430
This is very difficult,
because so many, like myself,

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.510
come from places where
you start with nothing.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.900
Half this audience came
from the fucking dirt,

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.660
the others had parents
or grandparents that did.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.740
This is deep within us that
once you tasted garbage,

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:48.300
you have no interest in
letting your children taste it.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.970
This is not judgment.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.570
You're looking at a man
whose run two companies now,

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.350
and the number one vulnerability I've had

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.220
running these two companies successfully

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.810
is I personally created
too much entitlement

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:02.080
with my organizations,
because I don't like conflict,

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.970
I struggle with radical candor.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.110
I'm a tough guy on fucking Instagram,

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.790
but in real life, I just
want to take all the pressure

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.095
and do it myself, and put
everybody in a happy place,

00:04:12.095 --> 00:04:15.120
'cause happiness deploys better success

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.700
until it over corrects.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.880
We have a whole culture that
is disproportionally judging

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.577
the youth, literally judging the youth

00:04:23.577 --> 00:04:26.250
that they fucking parented.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.730
My friends, for us to look
at this and understand

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.849
what's actually happening,
we have to understand

00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:35.836
that so many in today's
society, and long before social

00:04:35.836 --> 00:04:39.320
let us flex on each other,
we did it by the things

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.620
we wore, by the things we drove,

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.200
by the stories we told at the PTA.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.480
Most, most people continue
to parent their children

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.270
based on what they think
other people think of them,

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.573
not by listening to their actual children.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.300
This is a very important conversation.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.000
We cannot get to the path
of all the other talks

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.900
that we've been listening to without

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.790
eliminating entitlement.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:07.630
It is very difficult to
be empathetic or grateful

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.370
without eliminating entitlement.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.000
We must put accountability on a pedestal.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.770
We must destroy eighth place trophies.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.480
That doesn't mean that
we don't admire effort,

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.690
but results fucking matter in life.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.310
My mother gave me so
much fucking self esteem

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.180
that it makes some people not like me.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:32.240
However, she equaled
that with uncomfortable

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.910
amounts of accountability.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:36.070
When I went 0-4 in a baseball game,

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:39.840
and struck out four times,
it wasn't the sun's fault,

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.820
it wasn't my coach's fault.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.742
She looked me in the face and
said, "You fucking sucked."

00:05:44.742 --> 00:05:47.470
(audience laughing)

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:50.610
It didn't taste great,
it must've not been fun

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:55.560
for her to deliver, but
my deep, deep happiness

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.950
is predicated on her sucking
out every piece of entitlement

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.440
out of my body.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:05.530
My deep capacity to be
empathetic and grateful,

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.100
which transforms in what most people see

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:12.070
is somebody who markets, but
in the way I navigate my life,

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.210
and the way I market to the end consumer,

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.050
my unbelievable opportunity to speak

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:21.500
in front of this crowd today,
is predicated on listening.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.030
I talk, you listen to my podcast,

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.170
I interrupt every single
person that is on my show

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.860
because I've already heard what they said,

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.860
and I just want to move it
along, and we don't fucking edit.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.820
It seems mean, it seems audacious,

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.590
it's deeply based on listening.

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:42.180
We have to start the process
of listening to the youth.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.390
They're telling us the answers,

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:47.300
you just care what your
neighbor thinks about your kid,

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.200
you just care about what your
mother thinks about your kid,

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.810
you just care about what your
sister thinks about your kid.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.860
You need to start listening to your kid.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.350
When this little hub-bub that popped up

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.770
about USC and other colleges,
this was no surprise to me,

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.510
there was no shock behind this.

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:08.450
We are a mass society
predicated on overreacting

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.690
to other people's judgment.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.253
We are awfully good at judging,

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.800
we are awfully good at judging.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.150
We have to start the
conversation around entitlement.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:23.804
Entitlement's a tricky
one, it's a tricky one,

00:07:23.804 --> 00:07:26.130
because it's not a lot of fun for people

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.060
that are trying to do
good to really look at it.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:33.230
There's a whole lot of people
that clap for Greta's talk,

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.670
and then act a different way the next day.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.960
We all know that.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.760
The hypocrisy is fucking heavy.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.730
Some things are really lofty.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:45.100
It's hard to fucking boil
the ocean, but the truth is

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.630
you can absolutely start with yourself,

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:52.200
and let me promise you the
deep happiness in perpetuity

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.910
that you will have if
you start with your child

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.200
will change the course of your life.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.870
I've seen this up close with my siblings,

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.810
I've seen this through the
eyes of hundreds of thousands

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:07.820
of people who I've talked to yesterday.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:11.920
The resentment is palpable.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.842
More importantly, they genuinely believe

00:08:14.842 --> 00:08:17.060
that you do not believe in them

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.780
because you're subsidizing their behavior.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:23.870
Fake environments were
the seed that lead us

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.200
to the uncomfortable place were in,

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:30.610
predicated on an enormous
amount of money and happiness

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.170
in the macro over the last 70 years.

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.370
And much like in out venture community

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:38.030
where people no longer
actually build businesses,

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.610
but they're building
financial arbitrage machines

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.937
to raise capital and
spend zero fucking time

00:08:43.937 --> 00:08:48.330
caring about their consumer,
and 100% of their time

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.220
caring about venture
capitalists and press.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.040
We equally have a community of parents

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.010
worried about what other people think

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.030
instead of how their kids feel.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:02.410
It is also why the marketing
world is massively audacious.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.740
We are entitled to think
somebody wants to watch

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.863
our bullshit video just
'cause we fucking made it.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:14.290
We have to have a much,
much deeper conversation

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.500
about entitlement, and when we do,

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.740
all the other beautiful
words that have been spoken

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.521
in the last two days will
start to fall into place.

00:09:23.521 --> 00:09:25.686
Thank you.

00:09:25.686 --> 00:09:29.603
(audience applause)
Thank you.

